.TH LDAPLIST 1 "November 2026" "ldaplist 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ldaplist \- list entries from OpenLDAP and Active Directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ldaplist
.RB [ \-dlv ]
.RB [ \-h server[:port] ]
.RB [ \-M domainName ]
.RB [ \-N profileName ]
.RB [ \-a authenticationMethod ]
.RB [ \-P certifPath ]
.RB [ \-D bindDN ]
.RB [ \-w bindPassword ]
.RB [ \-j passwdFile ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-p | \-s | \-g | \-u ]
.RI [ database [ key ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A read-only LDAP directory listing utility written in C. Supports LDAPv3, OpenLDAP, Active Directory, simple binds, and Kerberos/GSSAPI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -d
Enable LDAP library diagnostics.
.TP
.B -l
Classic output (default).
.TP
.B -v
Verbose connection diagnostics.
.TP
.BI -h " server[:port]"
LDAP server. Port 636 selects LDAPS.
.TP
.BI -M " domainName"
DNS domain converted to a base DN, or an explicit base DN.
.TP
.BI -N " profileName"
Read /etc/ldaplist/profiles/NAME.conf.
.TP
.BI -a " method"
kerberos (default), simple, bind, anonymous, or gssapi.
.TP
.BI -P " certifPath"
CA certificate file or directory.
.TP
.BI -D " bindDN"
Simple-bind DN.
.TP
.BI -w " bindPassword"
Password argument; prefer -j.
.TP
.B -W
Prompt for the simple-bind password without echoing it. Selects simple bind unless -a was explicitly supplied.
.TP
.BI -j " passwdFile"
Read first line of password file.
.TP
.B -t
Tab-separated People columns: uid, firstname, lastname, mail, mobile.
.TP
.B -p
Search ou=People.
.TP
.B -s
Search ou=SUDOers.
.TP
.B -g
Search ou=Groups.
.TP
.B -u
Search ou=automount.
.TP
.B -y
Search ou=policies and display common OpenLDAP ppolicy and Active Directory fine-grained password-policy attributes. Does not calculate effective policy for an individual user.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Kerberos/GSSAPI is the default. Acquire a ticket with kinit; the current credential cache is used automatically. For simple bind, use -D with -W to prompt without echoing the password. Simple binds should use LDAPS and trusted CA validation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LDAPURI, LDAPLIST_BASE_DN, LDAPLIST_DOMAIN, LDAPLIST_PEOPLE_OU, LDAPLIST_SUDOERS_OU, LDAPLIST_GROUPS_OU, LDAPLIST_AUTOMOUNT_OU, LDAPLIST_POLICIES_OU.
